-- EQUIL_1D_COMPVD_WATER_GASCAP with scaled end-points set group by group,
-- to show how the equilibration takes the gas end-points SGL and SGU, and
-- SWL and SWU with them.  Capillary pressure is zero, so the contacts are
-- sharp: above the gas-oil contact at 2574 m lies the gas zone, between it
-- and the water-oil contact at 2624 m the oil zone, and below that the water
-- zone.  Cells not named keep the end-points of the saturation table, and
-- FILLEPS writes the end-points of every cell to the INIT file.
--
-- Gas cap (1-24):
--   1-3     no scaled end-points
--   4-6     SGU 0.90, below 1 - SWL = 0.99
--   7-9     SWL 0.20 and SGU 0.70, below 1 - SWL = 0.80
--   10-12   SWL 0.15 and SGU 0.95, above 1 - SWL = 0.85
--   13-15   SWL 0.25 with SGU from the table
--   16-18   SWL 0.12 and SGU 0.88 = 1 - SWL
--   19-21   SGL 0.05
--   22-24   no scaled end-points
-- Oil zone (25-34):
--   25      SGL 0.05, next to the gas-oil contact
--   26      no scaled end-points
--   27-28   SGL 0.05
--   29-30   SWL 0.20 and SGL 0.08
--   31      no scaled end-points
--   32-33   SWL 0.15
--   34      no scaled end-points
-- Water zone (35-40):
--   35      no scaled end-points
--   36      SGL 0.05 with SWU 1.0, so SGL exceeds 1 - SWU
--   37-38   SWU 0.90
--   39-40   SWU 0.90 and SGL 0.05
-- SWCR is raised with SWL where SWL would exceed the table's 0.20.
--
-- GAS_ENDPOINTS_COLUMN_NO_SGL_SGU is the same column without SGL and SGU.
-- There are no wells; the restart file at time zero holds the equilibrated
-- saturations and phase compositions.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUNSPEC
------------------------------------------------------------------------
TITLE
COMPOSITIONAL EQUILIBRATION WITH SCALED GAS END-POINTS
METRIC

